== CORRECTION appended 23:50, do not misread the two "s1 port counters" sections above ==
`sudo -n ovs-ofctl dump-ports s1` FAILED with "sudo: a password is required" and printed
nothing. sudoers grants NOPASSWD for ovs-vsctl / ifconfig / mnexec / ndtwin-lab /
ndtwin-p4-power ONLY -- ovs-ofctl is not in the list (see 17_harness_tool_probe_wrong.log).
Those two sections are therefore EMPTY BECAUSE THE QUERY FAILED, not because the counters
read zero. The independent proof that packets really flowed is the ping statistics in the
same block: 3000 packets transmitted, 3000 received, 0% loss over 33.5 s. The finding is
unaffected -- it rests on the ping, on `sflow []` x10 from ovs-vsctl (which DOES work), and
on the kernel's own `flows=0, counters=0` rate-loop lines.

